Algorithm 3: JoinSlide (G, xi, xj, Ji, ε, w)

Input : an adjacent graph G of dataset Y, two data points xi, xj in dataset X, the join window Ji of xi and two parameters ε, w

Output : the join window Jj of xj in Y

1 Q ← Ji is a priority queue, sorted in ascending order based on δ(yp, xj) for every yp ∈ Q;

2 if δ(Q.top(), xj) > ε then

3 Visit ← Ji;

4 while Q is not empty do

5 if δ(Q.top(), xj) ≤ ε then break;

6 u ← Q.pop();

7 for each v ∈ NG(u) \ Visit do

8 if δ(v, xj) < δ(u, xj) then

9 Q.push(v); Visit ← Visit ∪ {v};

10 while Q.size() > w do

11 remove the last element from Q;

12 if Q is empty then return Jj = Ø;

13 Jj ← {yp|yp ∈ Q ∧ δ(yp, xj) ≤ ε};

14 push all elements in Jj into an empty queue Q;

15 while Q is not empty do

16 yp ← Q.pop();

17 for each yq ∈ NG(yp) do

18 if yq∉Jj and δ(yq, xj) ≤ ε then

19 Q.push(v); Jj ← Jj ∪ {yq};

20 return Jj;
```

