Algorithm 6: kJoinSlide (G, xi, xj, Ji, k, w)

Input : an adjacent graph G of dataset Y, two data points xi, xj, the join result Ji of xi and two parameters k, w

Output : the k-join result Jj of xj in Y

1 Q ← Ji is a priority queue, sorted in ascending order based on δ(yp, xj) for every yp ∈ Q;

2 Visit ← Ji; mark each u ∈ Q unexplored;

3 while at least one of the elements in Q is unexplored do

4    u ← the first unexplored element in Q; mark u explored;

5    for each v ∈ NG(u) \ Visit do

6    push v into priority queue Q;

7    Visit ← Visit ∪ {v}; mark v unexplored;

8    while Q.size() > w do

9    remove the last element from Q;

10 return the first k elements in Q;
```
